WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Golgo 13, top secret episode.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.480
Only you can help him save the world.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:29.080
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.020
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.680
And I'm Joe.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:40.940
And you see, Sean, that's exactly what I was talking about last week with the back of the box is that they usually sound so much more dire, okay?

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.220
Only you can help him save the world is a lot better than it's only a video game.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.180
It's true. It's true.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:56.920
And also, the title Golgo 13 is how most people know this game, but it does have the subtitle top secret episode.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.060
And for some reason to me, that just screams like DLC.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:09.160
Yeah, no, I mean, it took me a while just to get it through my head what this IP is supposed to be.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:15.800
Like, I know that this is based on something, but there really isn't a lot of information about what it was.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.140
Yeah, so it's based on the popular manga in Japan.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:26.260
I'm quite certain, definitely in 1988, but probably even now still, not many people knew what Golgo 13 was.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:34.240
And so it's even weirder that they chose to, like, cover this whole thing under the, you know, popular manga thing when no one knew what it was.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.220
But Golgo 13, he's actually known as, like, Duke Togo or something like that.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:46.080
And he's an assassin who his objective is to destroy the leader of the Drek group.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.220
I don't know what the Drek group is.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:53.260
I don't know if they're, like, supposed to be Russians or just, like, bad people in general.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.480
Yeah, they're, like, the Spectre.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.900
And Golgo 13 is, like, the 007, right?

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:02.660
Yeah, well, I think they, it looks like they changed him from an assassin to being a spy in this, right?

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.440
Like, it was like, he's a hitman in the manga, right?

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:10.220
Right. And now he's a spy here because it's, like, the one thing they wanted to change to make it more family friendly.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.820
Oh, yeah. Because they still left a lot of other things in.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.980
And I heard that Golgo 13 is actually, like, a reference to the death of Jesus.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.640
Yeah. What you told me, so, okay, we had, like, a group chat going.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.200
And I asked, what's the game this week?

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.100
And Mike texted me, Golgotha 13.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.480
So I looked that up and I see nothing about a video game.

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.800
I just see a bunch of, like, Bible study things.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.000
And I was totally thrown through a loop.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.620
I had to look it up in a separate way.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.820
And I didn't even realize I texted you that.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.820
That's just me feeling guilty about, like, the weight of this video game on our shoulders.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.300
And the game is weird to describe, to give, like, an overview of, right?

00:02:54.320 --> 00:03:02.460
We've never quite had anything that tackled so many different genres and also tried to be, like, cinematic and plot driven all at once.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.500
Does anybody want to take a stab at, like, explaining this game?

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.860
Can I? I'll give it a go.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.640
And I'm sure we'll need other people to jump in because there's a lot going on here.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.040
And I think the biggest thing about this game is that it's very ambitious.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:24.620
Yeah. So without even talking about the plot at first, there are just, like, there are, like, seven different, like, styles of gameplay in here.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.640
But, you know, as far as the plot, you're playing as this assassin.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:39.560
And you're actually walking through a side-scrolling level, going into buildings and, like, getting recon, getting information from people about where to go next and who to find.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.760
And, you know, it's giving you, like, a very cohesive story to play through.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:55.800
And then it uses these different, you know, it uses, like, a shmup style and an on-rail shooter style as, like, little, like, the apparatus for telling the next part of the story.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.240
If that makes any sense.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.280
Like, it'll say, get to the helicopter to do this.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.160
And then suddenly you're in a shmup level.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:13.280
Yeah. So I don't know how cohesive it actually is because the story itself seems to be, like, if you just, if you were watching a movie but you just watched, like,

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:26.520
three random scenes, like, throughout it, there seems to be a bacteriological weapon that you have to, that has nothing to do with you.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.060
And it sort of sounds like Cassandra G is, like, a T-virus sort of thing.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.040
But then it just drops you into Berlin.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:40.640
Yeah, Berlin for no reason aside from the fact that, you know, this whole thing happened in New York.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.020
I don't really know what's going on, but it's got, yeah.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:56.320
Sorry. What I gathered from that beginning, the helicopter blowing up and the girl saying that, the girl telling you what happened was that it was blown up and, what is it, the CIA that they're calling them?

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.820
The CIA and the KGB.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:08.740
Yeah. The CIA thinks that the only person in the world who would have the accuracy to snipe out the pilot in this helicopter or something is you.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.880
Yeah. So you're trying to, like, clear your name?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:20.000
I think beyond all the little, all the little details in this game, it's doing its best to cover all the bases of a Cold War thriller.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:21.840
Yeah, I could see that.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.820
And to be honest, like, I admire the ambition in it.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:33.240
I really do. I want this to, I want other games to, like, take this and improve upon it greatly.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:35.820
But, like, take this formula a little bit.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:49.520
Yeah, because, I mean, if we're just going even off of the intro, before you ever even start playing or anything like that, I think it's one of the strongest intros we've ever had for an NES game, let alone, like, anything before 3D graphics.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:58.760
Like, it's very, you know, even that helicopter blowing up at the Statue of Liberty is so interesting and, like, makes you wonder, like, what happened and stuff like that.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:07.340
I don't know. I think that the intro to that other globetrotting shooty gun game was pretty good, too.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.360
Oh, Freedom Force you're talking about, right?

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.800
Yeah. Was it Freedom Force?

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:13.460
Yeah. Freedom Force was with the Zapper, though.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.220
But, yeah, it had a great intro.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.760
But I don't know. This one feels very cinematic.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:24.600
And even the game throughout has, like, cut scenes, you know, with dialogue boxes and everything like that.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.600
So I feel like it's got a lot of parts.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.380
And on paper, this sounds like an incredible game.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:37.620
I think the longer you play this game, the easier it, like, plays all of its cards to you.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:41.780
And you kind of realize, like, oh, this sounds awesome, but it doesn't play awesome.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:51.040
But I think that that start, even with that cool, like, bullet shot at the beginning and then the Golgo 13, like, title screen with him, with the flashes.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.300
I thought that was really stylish.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.260
Yeah, it's all got a cool look to it.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:01.860
Yeah. Even that, I think this might be what you're talking about, Mike, but that close-up of his eyes.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:05.400
And then you see, like, I don't know if you see, like, the barrel of the sniper or the barrel.

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.180
Right, that's exactly right. The scope of the sniper rifle go over his eye.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:10.480
That's exactly what I'm talking about. And it looks really anime to me.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.600
You know, it looks like it's straight out of anime.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:18.060
Going off of, like, just the stylish touches, I also did appreciate.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:21.820
It took me a while to recognize what they were trying to get across.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:30.620
But in, like, the first, like, cut scene, I guess, you're in an airport and you just hear these weird, like, whooshing sounds.

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:35.160
And I'm like, oh, wait, they're trying to make it sound like airplanes are taking off in the background.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:39.080
And I just thought, like, that's a cool thing to just try out.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:41.740
Yeah, it's more like waves crashing in the ocean.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:46.840
It's like it's so disturbing and, like, overbearing at times.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.560
And I'm not sure if it was quite something that just happened at the airport.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.100
I felt like I saw it pop up later again when you're in Greece.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.560
But maybe that was also during the airport and I just forget.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:01.240
Because you've got to go to the airport all over the place no matter where you travel to.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:10.080
But, yeah, I think even the sprite work in general for the cut scenes was more than I anticipated the NES being able to handle.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:17.100
Because you can only put so many different types of, like, color palettes and designs on screen at once.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:21.680
And it didn't feel like anything was empty or barren during the cut scenes.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:26.600
It even prompts the players for the next dialogue box and stuff like that.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.860
So there was no auto scroll or anything.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:33.020
There was animated mouth movements.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:45.400
And I also like the touch where, like, you have to choose to look behind you in order to talk to somebody.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:47.580
Everybody just pops up behind you.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:55.020
Yeah, I feel like that was just, like, a way to give you a reason to, like, show their little, like, five frames of animation.

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:58.860
Which looked pretty nice on the NES of your character turning around.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.720
But it was like, oh, we got to make sure we put that in there.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:07.900
So, like, every time you have to, like, start facing the camera and then choose to turn around to talk to the person.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:15.220
I think the only strange choice in terms of, like, style is when you switch between different types of levels.

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:18.320
Because that's just white text on black.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:21.300
And it just feels like a miss.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:22.380
You know, like, they could have added.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.440
Even Act 2 or Act 3, whenever it says that.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:26.900
It's just the text.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:31.700
And it feels like it could have been a chance for, like, a big reveal of the next location.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:34.520
Or, like, fancy sprite work of a helicopter.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:36.060
Like, we could have had things there.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:42.220
Yeah. Yeah, even, like, in the same style that they have that he's in the hotel looking around.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:49.100
You can have him, like, submerging in scuba gear underwater for, like, a couple of frames or something.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:52.600
Assuming that there's room to do that in this game.

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:59.600
There's also that cutscene in the hotel, though, like, somewhere in Act 2 that totally implies that he had sex with that woman.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:01.360
Yeah, I figured we would get to that.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:05.140
But, yeah, it seems like a couple of things have gotten past the radar here.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:07.120
There's some blood.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:14.400
Yeah, they even, like, okay, so you meet up with your contact or whoever it is.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:19.420
Maybe it's Cherry, one of the few named characters in the game.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:24.860
And she's like, I'm so happy you're here.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.580
And then it cuts to being outside of the building.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:34.600
And then you see a few pixels that are assumed to be you two.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:36.360
So they've come together.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.780
And then the window darkens.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:43.020
And then your life points go up very slowly.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.940
And then it's the next day.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:48.220
So it's pretty obvious what happened there.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:53.780
Yeah, I do think it's funny, too, that, like, oh, man, like, look at this, like, this dirty imagery.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:57.720
And it's, like, three pixels and three pixels, like, moving towards each other.

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:00.400
But it's just like, you're like, oh, I know what's going on here.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.760
And I thought I did know what was going on.

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:05.100
You know, I didn't think it was that bad, the sprite work.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:09.700
You know, I granted, like, they chose to make the scope of the hotel gigantic.

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:11.980
Tentic, but, like, I could tell that those were two people.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:14.300
No, I'm not saying that you couldn't tell.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:17.000
I'm just saying it was funny that, like, oh, this is, like, the dirty part.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:21.320
It's raunchy. And it's just, like, it's literally just, like, it is just, like, you could tell they're supposed to be humans.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.480
Six raunchy pixels. Tiniest pixels.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:08.340
All right. So moving away from the style, though, for a minute, I have to talk about my own experience of being so jazzed about this game from the start.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:15.700
And then immediately upon, like, starting gameplay, this is a very jank game.

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:18.700
And I was not impressed at all from the moment I started playing.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.820
I don't know if you guys felt the same.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:32.740
No, I agree. The horizontal action part of the game, which is basically just a basic side-scrolling shooter slash beat-em-up,

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:44.660
is it goes back to all the old mistakes that these games were making with weird jump mechanics and funky hitboxes.

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:50.220
And basically, like, you can't choose where you shoot.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:57.180
So all these guys are pretty much invulnerable to you unless you get them at, like, the exact moment that you need to.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:58.960
It's just not a fun experience.

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:04.160
Yeah. The weirdest thing to me is that the weirdest decision to me is that you can duck.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:08.600
Yeah. I don't know what you had ever used the duck for because while you're ducking, you can't shoot.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:15.660
And then to go along with that, almost all of your enemies duck or are too short to shoot unless you're ducking.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:21.720
So you just can't shoot half of them until they jump or stand up, which is, like, most of the side-scrolling levels.

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:30.300
And for a game that grounds itself in some form of realism, referencing the CIA and the KGB and, like, these detailed cutscenes,

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:34.540
these side-scrolling action levels feel very bare bones.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:38.020
I mean, there's only ever one enemy at a time for the most part.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:40.920
When they crouch, they're completely untouchable.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:50.660
So you need to do this leap in the air that is just unbelievably – like, that guy could dunk on any basketball net, the how high he jumps.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:56.460
And you have to perfectly dodge, like, all three of those bullets with timed jumps that you have no control over.

00:13:56.780 --> 00:14:01.260
And then maybe if they get back up, you can shoot them in the face and they die immediately.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:05.700
But there's – other than that, like – and keep in mind that's one enemy at a time.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:10.860
There's very little interaction with anything else that's going on in these stages.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:19.160
I mean, you meet up with some guys who give you clues and those clues are – the clue givers are identical to the look of the bad guys.

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:20.220
So how would you know?

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:24.140
You have to shoot them and then find out, like, oh, wait, that was a clue giver.

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:34.000
The only reward of these level layouts is because these levels are so long, when you actually travel to a new country, it just feels nice to see some new scenery.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:35.660
Yeah, definitely.

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:45.480
I think that the designs of the levels, like, wow, you do see a lot of Berlin and then a lot of Greece.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:49.060
They are nice, like, in a vacuum.

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:56.980
Like, if I weren't exposed to them for so long at a time, I think that it's a pretty good – these are pretty good graphics all around.

00:14:57.180 --> 00:15:01.780
Yeah, I think that – yeah, the whole game looks pretty good for the most part.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:07.960
And I just want to go back to what you were saying, Mike, about the, you know, the, like, lack of enemies on this screen and everything.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:13.940
I think for the side-scrolling stages, I would have been okay with it being, like, a slower thing because it's a spy thing.

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:19.580
And, like, just, you know, about testing your reflexes against, like, the first person you see, etc.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:24.640
If, first of all, you could control where you're shooting so you could actually hit these people.

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:36.840
And the other thing that would have made, I think, the side-scrolling game side part better is the fact that you – in the game, you can – you're going into these buildings and finding new clues, which I thought was kind of cool.

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:41.680
Except for the fact that there's absolutely no indication on which buildings you can go into and which you can't.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:45.300
So you have to completely guess where there are paths that you can go into.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:46.800
And there's, like – there's nothing.

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:50.960
It could be any step you're on, you might – you can try hitting up to see if you can go into that building.

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:53.760
I mean, there are some – there are some markers.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:58.620
Like, every – every underground station that you pass, you can go into that.

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:00.860
And then there are a couple buildings you can walk into.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:04.140
And, yeah, like, you are sort of pixel hunting for a while.

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:05.140
So, but –

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:07.800
The underground stations are the only ones that are, like, consistent, though.

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:11.440
There are some buildings that look the same as other buildings you can go in that you can't go in.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:17.240
But this is, like, a play space that you're going to be in for a while and you will eventually learn it.

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:24.460
Like, I knew which building was the Green Mansion after trying several others and failing.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:28.300
So, I mean, I'm not saying that that gives this game a pass.

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.480
I don't think that's correct.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.120
Right. And I might be misremembering, but I think there was at least one time where there was one –

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:41.020
it just looked like every other completely random building that I happened to hit up on it and I happened to go inside it.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:45.260
And I was like, well, that's never been the case for any of these other buildings that look like this, which there are a lot of.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:49.360
Yeah. So, that was a little bothering – bothersome to me.

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:52.440
Yeah. And just describe these level layouts a little bit.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:17:01.620
They're kind of like where in the world is Carmen Sandiego where, you know, when you first go to these new areas, you have, like, a lot to explore.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.360
But as Sean said, you become acquainted with it.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:11.460
So, I definitely understand what you mean when, like, it's rewarding when a clue says go to the Green Mansion and you know where that is.

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:14.000
Like, that's kind of – that's cool level processing.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:22.280
But at the same time, I think what Joe was getting at was that the first thing you're ever introduced to in this game is the idea of going down into those subways.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:28.100
And those felt very clear as like, oh, every time I come across one of those, I could probably go in those.

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:33.560
Like, they were inviting, whereas some of these other places that you have to go to don't necessarily read.

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:36.260
It was a problem in Rambo.

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.800
Remember, that was like a thing where, like, you wouldn't know.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.160
But this isn't as bad as Rambo.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:43.100
No, this is nowhere near as bad as Rambo.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:49.860
I do cede that it is an issue in communicating clearly to the player.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:53.640
But, yeah, it's nowhere near as bad as it has been before.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:56.680
And what's going on with those motorcycle enemies?

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.240
Like, what the heck is that about?

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.820
Yeah, a little out of place, I guess.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:04.260
You ever heard of the motorcycle games of Berlin and Athens?

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:06.560
That look exactly the same?

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:09.060
Yeah. I just don't get that.

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:16.160
It's like, you know, I could understand, like, the slow pace of the one-on-one gun duel that you're having and stuff like that.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:22.620
But then to just have these guys on motorcycles to just outright try to run you over just feels like you're in the wrong game, buddy.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:29.500
But some of the clue givers will also just not give you clues and just tell you how unwelcome you are there.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:33.220
So I think that that might be because of the gangs.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.280
Yeah, but that's just, you know, Russian culture.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:39.920
They want you to know that you're not welcome there.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:41.760
You're not in Russia.

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:47.380
Oh, sorry. I said Berlin, so I was thinking Russia for a minute.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.740
I'm thinking of the KGB part.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:50.980
Berlin is in Germany.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:52.720
No, I know. That's what I'm saying.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.600
I'm saying that I was mixing the KGB with Berlin.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:57.780
Yes, yes.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:06.980
Okay, cool. So we can move on to the FPS portion here because I don't even know if that's the right way to describe it per se.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:13.420
But it felt like this would have been the perfect zapper companion if that helps picture it for anybody at home.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:23.620
It really does look like your gun is drawn out and you have the crosshairs and then you have to like take down, depending on the level, helicopters, tanks, fighter jets.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:41.360
I thought this was all cool except for that it's tough to use that D-pad to lock on to enemy helicopters and other objects because they come by kind of in and out of the screen in this weird depth way where they try to like, you know, they get smaller and then they come up big and then they go small.

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:47.280
But it happens so quickly that if you're not like prepared for where they might be, you're going to have to take some time to track them down.

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:50.740
So those are my beefs with this section.

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:58.920
Yeah. So there are two different modes in this game that could be sort of described as the first person shooter mode.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:01.860
But he's talking about the pan and zoom mode.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:11.720
And as Joe described earlier, it's sort of closer to an on-rails shooter, but you get to control where you're looking.

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:16.060
I don't know if Joe has any more to say on that.

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:26.320
No. Yeah. I was just going to say it's almost kind of like you are looking through the eyes of your character now and you're just standing on the spot going left and right like in 360 degrees.

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:30.940
And then finding like where the enemies are in your peripherals.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:36.780
And it is kind of frustrating because you will get hit by things that are not on the screen.

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:40.020
Yeah. I noticed that it's particularly with the enemies on the ground.

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:48.520
Yeah. Maybe it was just the way I was noticing it, but I definitely felt like I had to get the enemies on the ground first because they're going to shoot me no matter where I'm looking.

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:53.520
But I don't remember ever getting shot after I killed all the enemies on the ground by something I wasn't looking at.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:21:01.220
Yeah. I will say, though, that at least this feels a bit more fair than the side scrolling parts.

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:03.800
Like if you do hit them, you hit them.

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:12.380
And there's no hitboxing that makes it so that they can just crouch and then you miss.

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:15.160
Yeah. This section grew on me a little bit.

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:21.080
At first, I wasn't crazy about it because it was a little annoying to use that D-pad to control the cursor.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:32.000
But once I kind of got used to it, it was actually a nice way because whenever you hit anything in the game in general, but particularly in these levels, you gain quite a bit of health.

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:40.400
Yeah. Like in the side scrolling, you might gain like 10 health, but in these levels, you gain like 80 health for everyone you hit.

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:46.260
So it was really just like a good way to kind of boost your health back up to the max, which is 200.

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:48.900
These sections also start very strange.

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:50.820
It almost feels like you've died.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:56.420
Yeah. When you're introduced to them, there's like this flash of red that comes across the screen.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:59.160
I think sometimes even a bullet pops up or something like that.

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.020
I can't remember what the visual cue.

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:04.180
It's like the cameraman's hand pops up.

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:05.840
And he shoots you. And he has a gun in it.

00:22:05.980 --> 00:22:08.300
Yeah. He shoots you. And that triggers it.

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:10.140
Yeah. Okay. And there's nothing you can do about it.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.880
It will happen when it's going to happen.

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:15.760
It's like simulating an ambush, but it happens so often.

00:22:16.720 --> 00:22:22.520
Yeah. And if you go back to a spot that it happened to you before, it'll happen again at that same

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:24.160
scene. And you do have to backtrack a little bit.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:27.480
So that can get a little annoying where you're like, I kind of already did this and I'm going

00:22:27.480 --> 00:22:31.400
to walk. You know, as soon as I walk on that pixel, it's going to happen again.

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:38.000
Are there any other thoughts on this, what I would have considered a great chance for the

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:39.980
zapper to make an appearance in this game?

00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:50.860
Bye.

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:41.400
If we move on, then it seems like the best thing to talk about next would be the thing

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:45.120
that follows afterwards, which is this shmup section of the game.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:51.460
And it's kind of weird to call it that because you're mostly dealing with like one enemy at

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:55.720
a time. Like it definitely gives you enough time from when an enemy appears on screens that you don't

00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:57.400
have to fight others at once.

00:23:57.600 --> 00:24:02.960
But when enemies do come on, some of them, like the fighter jets are so lightning fast

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:06.660
that for the most part, it's hard to tackle them as they come on the screen.

00:24:06.680 --> 00:24:08.840
And they're most likely going to hit you with their spread.

00:24:09.020 --> 00:24:12.640
I thought that was weird that not only are they fast, but they have this large spread

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:15.180
of like they can shoot six bullets at once.

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:20.940
And then there's also weird choices too of having certain enemies that aren't necessarily

00:24:20.940 --> 00:24:23.880
like things that we would find in our world.

00:24:24.020 --> 00:24:26.840
There was that thing with like the glowing orbs around it.

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:28.560
And I thought that was a strange choice.

00:24:29.020 --> 00:24:40.020
Yeah. So yeah, these segments are sort of like the bookends or like the interstitial moments between

00:24:41.460 --> 00:24:44.660
chapters or like you're going from one place to another.

00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:48.500
And so they just switch up the gameplay style again.

00:24:49.480 --> 00:24:56.120
But while you're in there, I think that like as opposed to a lot of the shmups that we played,

00:24:57.400 --> 00:25:03.640
because it's so bare bones, as you said, like you're way more focused on just dodging than

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:09.040
you are trying to take anybody down because you move so slowly that all you can really do

00:25:09.040 --> 00:25:10.480
is just make sure you don't get hit.

00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:17.160
And do you feel like Golgo 13, he's trying to prove something here by doing this all in

00:25:17.160 --> 00:25:21.460
a helicopter because he's being accused of shooting down that other helicopter?

00:25:21.840 --> 00:25:24.020
He's like, no, I would fly one any day.

00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:26.960
Yeah, he's trying to prove that he's pro-helicopter.

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:30.380
It just seems like it's a poor decision on his part.

00:25:30.520 --> 00:25:32.860
Those things just blew up over by the Statue of Liberty.

00:25:35.180 --> 00:25:40.120
There was a worldwide grounding of helicopters and he needed to prove.

00:25:40.620 --> 00:25:41.800
That it wasn't him.

00:25:42.380 --> 00:25:47.420
You're also, I don't know, I can't say for certain whether this happens at the other ones,

00:25:47.460 --> 00:25:53.280
but at the end of the first time that you do the shmup level, you're given a choice to

00:25:53.280 --> 00:25:59.100
like either approach or what they've defined as close up or snipe the enemy.

00:25:59.340 --> 00:26:02.460
And I think that that's pretty cool that, I mean, I only chose to snipe.

00:26:02.680 --> 00:26:03.820
Wait, that was a choice?

00:26:04.100 --> 00:26:06.840
I thought those were just controls for when you sniped.

00:26:07.440 --> 00:26:14.000
Oh, okay. I guess I was just pressing along and making it work because it does have the cursor go down.

00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:16.040
Yeah. Wow.

00:26:16.140 --> 00:26:18.700
Okay. Yeah. I guess I was doing it the same way as the game.

00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:20.100
I felt like I was in control.

00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:22.920
Yeah. Another moment of clip.

00:26:23.040 --> 00:26:24.580
No, no, no. You're controlling it.

00:26:24.580 --> 00:26:32.860
Like you, you control the, uh, uh, the scope and then you have to pixel hunt for the shooter.

00:26:33.140 --> 00:26:36.900
Right, right. So you're saying that approach and close up don't do anything other than snipe?

00:26:37.140 --> 00:26:42.260
I, uh, so I, I think what it was, was like you find like the window or wherever the, the

00:26:42.260 --> 00:26:43.200
shooter is. Right.

00:26:43.200 --> 00:26:49.220
And then when you, when you, when you zoom, it just, you're just locked in on, on the head

00:26:49.220 --> 00:26:50.480
of the target.

00:26:50.640 --> 00:26:51.720
And then you press the other button.

00:26:52.080 --> 00:26:53.840
You can't miss. Yeah. You can't move any direction.

00:26:54.280 --> 00:26:56.740
You're, you, he will just hit his target as soon as you press the button.

00:26:56.880 --> 00:26:58.640
Okay. Got it. Yeah.

00:26:58.760 --> 00:26:59.620
So that's just, yeah.

00:26:59.900 --> 00:27:02.140
Bad, bad clarity on the game's part again.

00:27:02.140 --> 00:27:06.580
Um, but yeah, that's like another hidden mode, like snipe mode.

00:27:06.740 --> 00:27:08.000
Like that's not even described.

00:27:08.420 --> 00:27:15.340
Yeah. It felt, it was another, another weird thing that we haven't seen before.

00:27:15.340 --> 00:27:20.360
So I, I appreciate those whenever we see them, no matter how poorly they're executed.

00:27:20.880 --> 00:27:24.940
And then next we have the scuba section of the game.

00:27:25.140 --> 00:27:27.020
Uh, something I wasn't expecting at all.

00:27:27.120 --> 00:27:29.940
I honestly did not think that they would, could add anything else.

00:27:29.940 --> 00:27:36.480
And, uh, this is definitely a lot better than, or more interesting, I should say, than anything

00:27:36.480 --> 00:27:41.240
else that, uh, I was dealing with so far in the game because there's multiple enemies.

00:27:41.380 --> 00:27:43.460
There's different layouts of the ocean floor.

00:27:43.640 --> 00:27:45.520
There's these caves to explore.

00:27:45.640 --> 00:27:48.280
Like you wouldn't think that you can go down into those pits.

00:27:48.400 --> 00:27:52.480
They look like bottomless pits that you would die if you fell into, but then they expose like

00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:56.880
a whole nother section of the underwater level that you have to go through those in order

00:27:56.880 --> 00:27:58.160
to find the secret bases.

00:27:58.780 --> 00:27:59.820
I love that.

00:27:59.980 --> 00:28:04.560
I love that you call it the ocean floor though, because this is just like, like some river

00:28:04.560 --> 00:28:07.260
flowing through Berlin that has sharks in it.

00:28:07.400 --> 00:28:09.140
I kind of, I kind of love that.

00:28:09.320 --> 00:28:13.600
It just, it seems like because there's nothing else around, like there's no, there's nothing

00:28:13.600 --> 00:28:18.300
above you. So it seems like you're in the ocean rather than like in some river.

00:28:18.580 --> 00:28:23.740
Oh, for sure. But like, yeah, every, every visual cue that they're giving you is telling you ocean.

00:28:24.200 --> 00:28:30.640
Yeah. But like, it's, it's just like that river would probably only be however, however deep.

00:28:30.780 --> 00:28:32.240
I don't know. It's just another cute thing.

00:28:32.620 --> 00:28:34.340
And it feels like you're going nowhere.

00:28:34.340 --> 00:28:38.400
So it is kind of easy to get lost if you're tracking around in here.

00:28:38.520 --> 00:28:42.800
You know, if you're just kind of like shooting down enemies as they come and going in a certain

00:28:42.800 --> 00:28:48.740
direction, it is possible to go in a circle or in the wrong direction and think you're heading

00:28:48.740 --> 00:28:51.300
in the right direction. I can't tell if I liked that or not.

00:28:51.520 --> 00:28:56.000
Yeah. I don't think, I don't think it's really, this game needs a component where you also

00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:59.560
need to start mapping on graph paper, but sure enough, that's coming up soon.

00:28:59.620 --> 00:29:02.040
So what were your guys' thoughts on the scuba level?

00:29:02.720 --> 00:29:06.960
I thought it was, I thought it was also like pretty good considering everything.

00:29:06.960 --> 00:29:12.640
I think it kind of is the same, the same way I feel about all of the other levels where

00:29:13.240 --> 00:29:17.380
I guess overall, I feel like this game is kind of a jack of all trades, master of none.

00:29:17.520 --> 00:29:20.180
Like it was, it was a fine underwater level.

00:29:20.660 --> 00:29:26.120
It didn't, as if it was a standalone underwater game, it would be, it would be very lacking.

00:29:26.340 --> 00:29:31.620
Yeah. I mean, I just appreciate that it, that its design was a bit more dense than the rest of

00:29:31.620 --> 00:29:40.360
the modes, but it's so short and it's not like it did dense in terms of like enemy, enemy

00:29:40.360 --> 00:29:49.720
and mine placement and like how the backgrounds look, but it's still a very simple thing and

00:29:49.720 --> 00:29:52.480
I wouldn't want to play more scuba.

00:29:53.840 --> 00:30:02.760
Yeah. And I did like also that they brought back the, the little on rail shooter section.

00:30:02.900 --> 00:30:07.220
Like you could just be swimming along and there's a little explosion and suddenly now you're in

00:30:07.220 --> 00:30:13.340
like an underwater on rails thing shooting at like, what are these like submarines and scuba

00:30:13.340 --> 00:30:15.300
divers instead of helicopters and.

00:30:15.440 --> 00:30:19.480
I believe they use for them is the frogmen core.

00:30:19.800 --> 00:30:21.060
Oh yeah. Yeah.

00:30:21.720 --> 00:30:22.560
Okay. Of course.

00:30:22.760 --> 00:30:25.400
Just so you know. Are the frogmen part of the Drek army?

00:30:26.500 --> 00:30:29.900
Yeah. They appear from the rear firing underwater spear guns.

00:30:30.400 --> 00:30:31.340
Got it. Okay.

00:30:31.860 --> 00:30:36.280
You know, I would say though, as we're working through all these modes, it's really cool that

00:30:36.280 --> 00:30:40.780
all these things are popping up, but also like thematically, it's pretty impressive.

00:30:40.780 --> 00:30:46.960
The idea that you went from like doing some investigative research in Berlin to then like, okay,

00:30:46.960 --> 00:30:53.320
cool. I get involved in a shootout with some helicopters to then finding out what you have to do next,

00:30:53.640 --> 00:31:00.360
meeting up with a girl in a hotel room, then boarding a helicopter and, and taking down

00:31:00.360 --> 00:31:02.560
enemy fighter jets and stuff like that.

00:31:02.740 --> 00:31:07.960
Sniping a guy going underwater to scuba dive to find a secret base.

00:31:07.980 --> 00:31:09.460
Like it's all cool stuff.

00:31:09.460 --> 00:31:11.120
It just sucks that it's not good.

00:31:11.760 --> 00:31:13.500
Yeah. Although, yeah, I agree though.

00:31:13.580 --> 00:31:16.280
It feels like it's like a James Bond movie.

00:31:16.400 --> 00:31:19.800
Like you're going to all these different like action set pieces, quote unquote.

00:31:20.020 --> 00:31:25.820
It's like uncharted. But you go to all these little different like action set pieces and you, and you play in

00:31:25.820 --> 00:31:30.660
different styles and you know, it's just, it feels like you're on like this long mission.

00:31:30.760 --> 00:31:35.960
That's like an actual like evolving mission.

00:31:35.960 --> 00:31:38.360
That's not just like the same thing over and over again.

00:31:38.480 --> 00:31:44.340
Because James Bond, or I'm sorry, Duke Togo, I'm sure in the manga doesn't just shoot guys.

00:31:44.340 --> 00:31:51.500
He's also a womanizer and he's also a professional helicopter pilot and he's also a really good,

00:31:51.500 --> 00:31:52.860
good like maze.

00:31:54.260 --> 00:31:55.520
He's really good at mazes.

00:31:55.940 --> 00:31:59.520
I don't know if any, if anything in this show that he was really good at mazes, but.

00:31:59.620 --> 00:32:00.480
Well, you're just playing.

00:32:00.560 --> 00:32:01.840
At least not the way I played it.

00:32:03.000 --> 00:32:07.780
I was playing for like a, like a more, a little more bad at mazes play style, you know?

00:32:07.880 --> 00:32:10.420
Yeah, for sure. That's like the character I was going with.

00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:16.300
The next thing that happens after you get to the base though, is, is the maze section

00:32:16.300 --> 00:32:20.740
of the game, which is first person, which is what Sean was alluding to is the second

00:32:21.960 --> 00:32:23.780
first person part of this game.

00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:27.940
But like what, where the heck did this come from?

00:32:28.180 --> 00:32:33.280
And did anybody else like imagine like that this was going to happen when they entered the

00:32:33.280 --> 00:32:37.360
base? I was expecting what, what also happens when you're in the bases, which is the side

00:32:37.360 --> 00:32:38.180
scrolling part.

00:32:38.180 --> 00:32:43.260
But then when I switched to this first person thing that was kind of like, um, Goonies 2

00:32:43.260 --> 00:32:46.860
esque where you have to like, you know, you don't, thankfully you don't have to select

00:32:46.860 --> 00:32:49.520
like moving forward and stuff like that for each thing.

00:32:49.640 --> 00:32:52.460
Or just like, I guess you do have to randomly do stuff though.

00:32:52.600 --> 00:32:54.760
Like who thought about the grenades to blow up the walls?

00:32:54.860 --> 00:32:56.120
I had to watch a video for that.

00:32:56.180 --> 00:32:57.540
Yeah. No, it took me some time.

00:32:57.540 --> 00:33:00.540
I just pressed the button and it worked just by accident.

00:33:00.820 --> 00:33:06.140
But, but I will say initially seeing this, like the actual first person element of it

00:33:06.140 --> 00:33:09.100
was pretty well executed for an NES game.

00:33:09.400 --> 00:33:14.480
This reminds me of, uh, like either, I forgot if it was Doom or if it was Wolfenstein for

00:33:14.480 --> 00:33:22.220
the TI-84, uh, just in, in terms of how you navigate, uh, it, it, because it's so simple,

00:33:22.220 --> 00:33:23.260
uh, looking.

00:33:23.260 --> 00:33:29.700
But I mean, I, what, what I, what I meant to say is I kind of wish that for this game,

00:33:29.780 --> 00:33:35.660
I did not read the manual because I wanted to be surprised by this, but I already knew

00:33:35.660 --> 00:33:43.980
it was coming. And they even have the, the, the whole map for the maze, uh, like written out for you

00:33:43.980 --> 00:33:45.140
at the back of the manual.

00:33:45.400 --> 00:33:50.240
So that was, it was just unfortunate, uh, my experience.

00:33:50.240 --> 00:33:55.140
Now I didn't read the manual, so I actually wasn't using the map.

00:33:55.640 --> 00:33:57.100
Oh, I wasn't reading the map either.

00:33:57.100 --> 00:33:58.260
Didn't even think that there would be one in there. Okay.

00:33:58.420 --> 00:34:03.500
Yeah. Cause I, cause, cause as much as I thought this was a cool idea to do, and even though

00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:06.920
it is like, yeah, the gameplay, maybe they could have like told you a few things on like

00:34:06.920 --> 00:34:10.340
what to do and like how to shoot or how to throw your grenades or everything.

00:34:10.780 --> 00:34:16.200
But, uh, this was like, I don't know if they needed to make this quite as complex of

00:34:16.200 --> 00:34:19.100
a maze with no landmarks or anything.

00:34:19.980 --> 00:34:22.920
Cause it was like, there are like two levels and

00:34:23.720 --> 00:34:25.520
it took me forever to get out of this thing.

00:34:25.680 --> 00:34:31.420
And I guess like it needed a, it needed a bit of a bigger payoff or change of scenery for

00:34:31.420 --> 00:34:32.940
like resolution of these things.

00:34:33.060 --> 00:34:34.380
Cause you keep going through them.

00:34:34.720 --> 00:34:35.920
Uh, and for the most

00:34:35.920 --> 00:34:39.700
part, you're just greeted by the same kind of like grunt who you have to shoot and knock

00:34:39.700 --> 00:34:43.960
out or blow up a wall that you hope has a hole in it.

00:34:44.060 --> 00:34:44.980
So this way you can go through

